findVariantCaseFieldTy(baseTy, self.fieldAccessName(fieldObj), expr->kind.payload.DerefField.field);\n                    if (ft == 0) return false;\n                    self.setExprType(id, self.substituteFieldTy(ft, baseTy));\n                    return true;\n                }\n            }\n            MemberInfo member = self.findMember(self.exprType(expr->kind.payload.DerefField.obj), expr->kind.payload.DerefField.field);\n            if (member.typeNode == 0) return false;\n            self.setExprType(id, self.substituteFieldTy(member.typeNode, self.exprType(expr->kind.payload.DerefField.obj)));\n            return true;\n        }\n        if (expr->kind.tag == ExprKind::Index)\n        {\n            if (!self.checkExpr(expr->kind.payload.Index.obj)) return false;\n            Ty objectType = self.exprType(expr->kind.payload.Index.obj);\n            if (objectType == 0) return false;\n            TypeEntry* objectEntry = self.ctx->types + objectType;\n            if (objectEntry->kind.tag == TypeKind::Array) self.setExprType(id, objectEntry->kind.payload.Array.base);\n            else if (objectEntry->kind.tag == TypeKind::Slice) self.setExprType(id, objectEntry->kind.payload.Slice.base);\n            else if (objectEntry->kind.tag == TypeKind::Pointer) self.setExprType(id, objectEntry->kind.payload.Pointer.base);\n            else return false;\n            return self.checkExpr(expr->kind.payload.Index.index);\n        }\n        if (expr->kind.tag == ExprKind::Deref)\n        {\n            if (!self.checkExpr(expr->kind.payload.Deref.expr)) return false;\n            Ty pointerType = self.exprType(expr->kind.payload.Deref.expr);\n            if (pointerType == 0) return false;\n            TypeEntry* pointerEntry = self.ctx->types + pointerType;\n            if (pointerEntry->kind.tag != TypeKind::Pointer) return false;\n            self.setExprType(id, pointerEntry->kind.payload.Pointer.base);\n            return true;\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    /* a call through a function-pointer value (parameter, local, field):\n     * arity + argument types + result type all come from the FnPtr type */\n    bool checkFnPtrCall(NodeId callId, Ty calleeTy, NodeId* args, u32 argsLen)\n    {\n        if (calleeTy == 0) return true;\n        TypeEntry* te = self.ctx->types + calleeTy;\n        while (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Const || te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Comptime)\n        {\n            if (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Const) te = self.ctx->types + te->kind.payload.Const.base;\n            else te = self.ctx->types + te->kind.payload.Comptime.base;\n        }\n        if (te->kind.tag != TypeKind::FnPtr) return true;\n        if (argsLen != te->kind.payload.FnPtr.paramsLen)\n        {\n            String msg = String::new();\n            msg.pushView(\"wrong number of arguments in function-pointer call: expected \");\n            self.pushDec(&msg, (u64)te->kind.payload.FnPtr.paramsLen);\n            msg.pushView(\", got \");\n            self.pushDec(&msg, (u64)argsLen);\n            self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaArityMismatch, callId, msg.asView());\n            return false;\n        }\n        u32 i = 0;\n        while (i < argsLen)\n        {\n            if (!self.checkAssign(args[i], self.exprType(args[i]), te->kind.payload.FnPtr.params[i]))\n                self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaTypeMismatch, args[i],\n                    self.typeMismatchMsg(\"argument type\", self.exprType(args[i]), te->kind.payload.FnPtr.params[i]));\n            i++;\n        }\n        self.setExprType(callId, te->kind.payload.FnPtr.returnType);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    bool checkCall(NodeId callId, Str name, NodeId* args, u32 argsLen, Ty calleeTy)\n    {\n        Symbol* symbol = self.lookupAt(name, callId);\n        if (symbol == null)\n        {\n            String msg = String::new();\n            msg.pushView(\"call to undeclared function '\");\n            msg.pushView(self.nameTextView(name));\n            msg.pushView(\"'\");\n            self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaUndeclaredIdent, callId, msg.asView());\n            return false;\n        }\n        /* A type name in call position is not a constructor in Coral:\n         * `Spaces(10)` used to slip through as a fn-pointer call and only\n         * fail later in gcc. Construct structs with a literal, or call the\n         * lowercase constructor helper. */\n        if (symbol->kind == 3 && argsLen > 0)\n        {\n            String msg = String::new();\n            msg.pushView(\"type '\");\n            msg.pushView(self.nameTextView(name));\n            msg.pushView(\"' is not callable\");\n            self.semaErrorNodeHelp(ErrorCode::SemaTypeMismatch, callId, msg.asView(),\n                \"construct a struct with `Type { .field = value }`, or call a constructor function such as `spaces(n)`\");\n            return false;\n        }\n        return self.checkCallResolved(callId, symbol, args, argsLen, calleeTy);\n    }\n\n    /* checkCall with the callee already resolved: qualified calls\n     * (`fios::fileOpen`) resolve the symbol in the module's file first,\n     * which bare name lookup cannot do when this file declares the same\n     * name (`fs.crl` has its own `fileOpen`) */\n    bool checkCallResolved(NodeId callId, Symbol* symbol, NodeId* args, u32 argsLen, Ty calleeTy)\n    {\n        Node* declNode = self.ctx->nodes + symbol->declaration.index;\n        if (declNode->kind.tag != NodeKind::Decl) return self.checkFnPtrCall(callId, calleeTy, args, argsLen);\n        Decl* decl = &declNode->kind.payload.Decl.value;\n        if (decl->kind.tag != DeclKind::Func) return self.checkFnPtrCall(callId, calleeTy, args, argsLen);\n        u32 paramsLen = decl->kind.payload.Func.paramsLen;\n        bool variadic = false;\n        if (paramsLen > 0)\n        {\n            NodeId lastParamId = decl->kind.payload.Func.params[paramsLen - 1];\n            Node* lastParamNode = self.ctx->nodes + lastParamId.index;\n            if (lastParamNode->kind.tag == NodeKind::Param)\n            {\n                Param* lastParam = &lastParamNode->kind.payload.Param.value;\n                if ((lastParam->flags & 16) != 0)\n                {\n                    variadic = true;\n                    paramsLen--;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        if (argsLen < paramsLen || (!variadic && argsLen != paramsLen))\n        {\n            String msg = String::new();\n            msg.pushView(\"wrong number of arguments in call to '\");\n            msg.pushView(self.nameTextView(decl->kind.payload.Func.name));\n            msg.pushView(\"': expected \");\n            self.pushDec(&msg, (u64)paramsLen);\n            if (variadic) msg.pushView(\" or more\");\n            msg.pushView(\", got \");\n            self.pushDec(&msg, (u64)argsLen);\n            self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaArityMismatch, callId, msg.asView());\n            return false;\n        }\n        /* C++/clang template rule: explicit typeargs on the callee\n         * (`zero<E<i32, i32>>(p, n)`) bind the generic params once, then\n         * arguments are checked against the SUBSTITUTED parameter types;\n         * concrete sameType compares, no dependent-vs-dependent shape\n         * walking. Bound once here and reused for the args and retTy. */\n        u32 sflag = 0;\n        if (decl->kind.payload.Func.genericParamsLen > 0 && calleeTy != 0)\n        {\n            TypeEntry* ce = self.ctx->types + calleeTy;\n            if (ce->kind.tag == TypeKind::Named && ce->kind.payload.Named.genericArgsLen == decl->kind.payload.Func.genericParamsLen)\n            {\n                sflag = 1;\n            }\n        }\n        /* a generic call with no explicit typeargs must be inferable by\n         * mono from direct parameter positions; otherwise no instance is\n         * ever collected (G0002) and codegen runs on a phantom call */\n        if (decl->kind.payload.Func.genericParamsLen > 0 && sflag == 0)\n        {\n            u32 gcount = decl->kind.payload.Func.genericParamsLen;\n            u8* slots = alloc<u8>((usize)gcount);\n            if (slots != null)\n            {\n                zero<u8>(slots, (usize)gcount);\n                self.markInferableGenericSlots(decl, argsLen, slots);\n                u32 gi = 0;\n                while (gi < gcount)\n                {\n                    if (slots[gi] == 0)\n                    {\n                        Node* gpn = self.ctx->nodes + decl->kind.payload.Func.genericParams[gi].index;\n                        String msg = String::new();\n                        msg.pushView(\"cannot infer generic type argument `\");\n                        if (gpn->kind.tag == NodeKind::GenericParam)\n                            msg.pushView(self.nameTextView(gpn->kind.payload.GenericParam.value.name));\n                        else msg.pushView(\"?\");\n                        msg.pushView(\"` in call to '\");\n                        msg.pushView(self.nameTextView(decl->kind.payload.Func.name));\n                        msg.pushView(\"' from the argument types\");\n                        self.semaErrorNodeHelp(ErrorCode::SemaBrokenDeclaration, callId, msg.asView(),\n                            \"pass the type explicitly, e->g. `callee<i32>(...)` or make it a comptime generic to have inference.\");\n                        dealloc<u8>(slots);\n                        return false;\n                    }\n                    gi++;\n                }\n                dealloc<u8>(slots);\n            }\n        }\n        u32 i = 0;\n        while (i < argsLen)\n        {\n            /* a `...pack` spread consumes the variadic tail; no per-slot\n             * check against a fixed param */\n            Node* argNode = self.ctx->nodes + args[i].index;\n            bool isSpread = argNode != null && argNode->kind.tag == NodeKind::Expr &&\n                            argNode->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.tag == ExprKind::Spread;\n            if (isSpread)\n            {\n                if (!self.checkExpr(args[i])) return false;\n                i++;\n                continue;\n            }\n            if (i < paramsLen)\n            {\n                NodeId paramId = decl->kind.payload.Func.params[i];\n                Node* paramNode = self.ctx->nodes + paramId.index;\n                if (paramNode->kind.tag == NodeKind::Param)\n                {\n                    Param* param = &paramNode->kind.payload.Param.value;\n                    if (!self.genericArgParam(decl, param))\n                    {\n                        Ty want = param->typeNode;\n                        if (sflag == 1) want = self.substituteFieldTy(want, calleeTy);\n                        if (!self.checkAssign(args[i], self.exprType(args[i]), want))\n                        {\n                            if (param->name != 0)\n                                self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaTypeMismatch, args[i],\n                                    self.paramMismatchMsg(param->name, self.exprType(args[i]), want));\n                            else\n                                self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaTypeMismatch, args[i],\n                                    self.typeMismatchMsg(\"argument type\", self.exprType(args[i]), want));\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            i++;\n        }\n        /* explicit typeargs on the callee (`realloc<cchar>(p, n)`); substitute\n         * the generic params in the return type so downstream sees the\n         * concrete pointer type instead of an unresolved `T*` */\n        Ty retTy = decl->kind.payload.Func.returnType;\n        if (sflag == 1)\n            retTy = self.substituteFieldTy(retTy, calleeTy);\n        self.setExprType(callId, retTy);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    /* `a::b::c` path minus the last segment, joined back with `::`;\n     * the module path an use-path match is tested against */\n    Str modulePathPrefix(NodeId* segs, u32 segCount)\n    {\n        if (segs == null || segCount < 2) return 0;\n        u32 keep = segCount - 1;\n        usize totalLen = 0;\n        u32 i = 0;\n        while (i < keep)\n        {\n            Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + segs[i].index;\n            if (n->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr || n->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.tag != ExprKind::Ident) return 0;\n            InternEntry* e = self.ctx->interns + n->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.payload.Ident.name;\n            if (i > 0) totalLen += 2;\n            totalLen += e->len;\n            i++;\n        }\n        u8* buf = alloc<u8>(totalLen);\n        if (buf == null) return 0;\n        usize w = 0;\n        i = 0;\n        \n        while (i < keep)\n        {\n            Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + segs[i].index;\n            InternEntry* e = self.ctx->interns + n->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.payload.Ident.name;\n            if (i > 0) { buf[w] = 58; buf[w + 1] = 58; w += 2; }\n            usize k = 0;\n            while (k < e->len) { buf[w] = e->ptr[k]; w++; k++; }\n            i++;\n        }\n        Str out = self.ctx->intern(str { .ptr = buf, .len = w });\n        dealloc<u8>(buf);\n        return out;\n    }\n\n    bool checkPath(NodeId id)\n    {\n        if (id.index == 0) return true;\n        Node* node = self.ctx->nodes + id.index;\n        if (node->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return true;\n        Expr* expr = &node->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (expr->kind.tag != ExprKind::Path) return true;\n        NodeId* segments = expr->kind.payload.Path.segments;\n        u32 segmentsLen = expr->kind.payload.Path.segmentsLen;\n        if (segmentsLen < 2) return true;\n        Node* leftNode = self.ctx->nodes + segments[0].index;\n        if (leftNode->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return true;\n        Expr* leftExpr = &leftNode->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (leftExpr->kind.tag == ExprKind::Path) return self.checkPath(segments[0]);\n        if (leftExpr->kind.tag == ExprKind::TypeRef)\n        {\n            // `Option<f64>::None`: type of the path is the head type\n            self.setExprType(id, leftExpr->kind.payload.TypeRef.typeNode);\n            return true;\n        }\n        if (leftExpr->kind.tag != ExprKind::Ident) return true;\n        Node* rightNode = self.ctx->nodes + segments[1].index;\n        if (rightNode->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return true;\n        Expr* rightExpr = &rightNode->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (rightExpr->kind.tag != ExprKind::Ident) return true;\n        Str root = leftExpr->kind.payload.Ident.name;\n        Str member = rightExpr->kind.payload.Ident.name;\n        Symbol* symbol = self.lookupAt(root, id);\n        if (symbol == null)\n        {\n            String msg = String::new();\n            msg.pushView(\"undeclared module '\");\n            msg.pushView(self.nameTextView(root));\n            msg.pushView(\"' in path\");\n            self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaUndeclaredIdent, id, msg.asView());\n            return false;\n        }\n        // enum value: Color::Red; type is the enum itself\n        if (symbol->declaration.index != 0)\n        {\n            Node* edeclNode = self.ctx->nodes + symbol->declaration.index;\n            if (edeclNode->kind.tag == NodeKind::Decl && edeclNode->kind.payload.Decl.value.kind.tag == DeclKind::Enum)\n            {\n                Decl* edecl = &edeclNode->kind.payload.Decl.value;\n                self.setExprType(id, self.namedType(edecl->kind.payload.Enum.name));\n                return true;\n            }\n            // bare variant: Option::None; type is the variant decl\n            if (edeclNode->kind.tag == NodeKind::Decl && edeclNode->kind.payload.Decl.value.kind.tag == DeclKind::Variant)\n            {\n                Decl* edecl = &edeclNode->kind.payload.Decl.value;\n                self.setExprType(id, self.namedType(edecl->kind.payload.Variant.name));\n                return true;\n            }\n        }\n        if (symbol->kind == 5 && symbol->declaration.index != 0)\n        {\n            Node* declNode = self.ctx->nodes + symbol->declaration.index;\n            if (declNode->kind.tag == NodeKind::Decl)\n            {\n                Decl* decl = &declNode->kind.payload.Decl.value;\n                if (!self.moduleExportsContain(decl, member))\n                {\n                    self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaUnknownMember, id, \"symbol not exported by module\");\n                    return false;\n                }\n                if (!self.moduleMemberIsPub(declNode, member))\n                {\n                    self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaUnknownMember, id, \"symbol not exported by module\");\n                    return false;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    /* TC-0009: an integer (literal or typed) is never a pointer. Always\n     * reported; --allow-int-ptr keeps it non-fatal, -w silences it. */\n    void intToPtrDiag(NodeId value)\n    {\n        if (self.diag == null) return;\n        SourceLoc loc;\n        loc.data = 0;\n        if (value.index != 0)\n        {\n            Node* node = self.ctx->nodes + value.index;\n            loc = node->loc;\n        }\n        if (self.allowIntPtr) self.diag->emitAllowed(ErrorCode::SemaIntToPtr, loc, \"cannot assign an integer to a pointer\", \"use `null` for a null pointer, or cast the integer explicitly\");\n        else self.semaError(ErrorCode::SemaIntToPtr, loc, \"cannot assign an integer to a pointer\");\n    }\n\n    /* A positional brace literal `{ a, b }` only makes sense for an\n     * aggregate target. Untyped literals otherwise have type 0, which\n     * compatible() accepts for any target, so `char c = { 'a', 'b' }`\n     * used to reach codegen and emit a bogus scalar initializer. */\n    bool braceInitTarget(Ty ty)\n    {\n        while (ty != 0)\n        {\n            TypeEntry* te = self.ctx->types + ty;\n            if (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Const) ty = te->kind.payload.Const.base;\n            else if (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Comptime) ty = te->kind.payload.Comptime.base;\n            else break;\n        }\n        if (ty == 0) return false;\n        TypeEntry* te = self.ctx->types + ty;\n        switch (te->kind.tag)\n        {\n            TypeKind::Array | TypeKind::Slice | TypeKind::Tuple | TypeKind::Named => { return true; },\n            else => { return false; },\n        }\n    }\n\n    bool isBraceLiteral(NodeId value)\n    {\n        if (value.index == 0) return false;\n        Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + value.index;\n        return n->kind.tag == NodeKind::Expr && n->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.tag == ExprKind::ArrayLiteral;\n    }\n\n    bool assignCompatible(NodeId value, Ty fromTy, Ty targetTy)\n    {\n        if (targetTy != 0 && self.isBraceLiteral(value) && !self.braceInitTarget(targetTy)) return false;\n        if (self.compatible(fromTy, targetTy)) return true;\n        /* char literals are untyped codepoint constants and fit the\n         * one-byte C types the same way small int literals do\n         * (`u8 b = 'x'`, `tmp[0] = '0'`); a char VALUE is UTF-32 and\n         * still needs an explicit cast to narrow */\n        if (value.index != 0 && targetTy != 0 && self.isCharLitNode(value) && self.charFamily(targetTy))\n            return true;\n        /* compile-time constant int expressions (`16 + 1`, `'a' - 1`) are\n         * generic; they adopt the expected integer target type at the use\n         * site, same as a bare literal. Without this, `alloc(16 + 1)` types\n         * the literal-sum as i32 and rejects a usize param. */\n        if (value.index != 0 && self.integerType(targetTy) && self.isConstIntExpr(value))\n        {\n            /* a `u`-suffixed literal stays unsigned-only even inside a\n             * compound const-int expr (`5u + 1`), matching the bare-literal\n             * rule further down; the fast path must not launder it into a\n             * signed target during ternary branch unification either */\n            if (self.hasUnsignedSuffix(value)) return !self.intSigned(targetTy);\n            self.setExprType(value, targetTy);\n            return true;\n        }\n        /* tuple literals adopt the expected element types: `((u32)b0, 1)`\n         * in a `(u32, u32)` return can't be seen by compatible() alone */\n        if (fromTy != 0 && targetTy != 0 && value.index != 0)\n        {\n            TypeEntry* fte = self.ctx->types + fromTy;\n            TypeEntry* tte = self.ctx->types + targetTy;\n            if (fte->kind.tag == TypeKind::Tuple && tte->kind.tag == TypeKind::Tuple &&\n                fte->kind.payload.Tuple.elemsLen == tte->kind.payload.Tuple.elemsLen)\n            {\n                Node* vn = self.ctx->nodes + value.index;\n                if (vn->kind.tag == NodeKind::Expr && vn->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.tag == ExprKind::TupleExpr)\n                {\n                    bool ok = true;\n                    u32 ti = 0;\n                    while (ti < tte->kind.payload.Tuple.elemsLen)\n                    {\n                        NodeId elemId = vn->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.payload.TupleExpr.elems[ti];\n                        Ty want = tte->kind.payload.Tuple.elems[ti];\n                        if (!self.assignCompatible(elemId, self.exprType(elemId), want)) { ok = false; break; }\n                        self.setExprType(elemId, want);\n                        ti++;\n                    }\n                    if (ok)\n                    {\n                        self.setExprType(value, targetTy);\n                        return true;\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        // integer/float literal initializers convert when the value fits\n        if (value.index != 0)\n        {\n            Node* vn = self.ctx->nodes + value.index;\n            if (vn->kind.tag == NodeKind::Expr)\n            {\n                Expr* ev = &vn->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n                /* `-1` parses as Neg{ IntLit }; unwrap the sign so\n                 * negated literals get the same literal leniency, with\n                 * signed range limits (magnitude, sign-aware) */\n                bool negated = false;\n                if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Neg)\n                {\n                    NodeId negIn = ev->kind.payload.Neg.expr;\n                    if (negIn.index != 0)\n                    {\n                        Node* nin = self.ctx->nodes + negIn.index;\n                        if (nin->kind.tag == NodeKind::Expr)\n                        {\n                            ev = &nin->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n                            negated = true;\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n                if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::IntLit)\n                {\n                    u64 v = ev->kind.payload.IntLit.value;\n                    bool unsignedSuffix = (ev->kind.payload.IntLit.flags & 1) != 0;\n                    TypeEntry* te = targetTy != 0 ? self.ctx->types + targetTy : null;\n                    if (te != null)\n                    {\n                        /* `T* p = 0`: an integer literal is not a pointer;\n                         * pure rejection here, checkAssign reports TC-0009 */\n                        if (self.pointerLike(targetTy)) return false;\n                        /* an int literal only ever adopts an integer (or\n                         * float) target. A struct/slice/str target is a\n                         * hard mismatch: `sleepTimespec(10000u)` used to\n                         * slip past the unsigned rule below, whose\n                         * intSigned() is false for every non-int type */\n                        if (!self.integerType(targetTy) && !self.floatType(targetTy))\n                            return false;\n                        /* `u`-suffixed literal: unsigned-only. Rejects any\n                         * signed target type regardless of value; `1u` is\n                         * generic among unsigned types (u8..u64, usize). */\n                        if (unsignedSuffix) return !self.intSigned(targetTy);\n                        switch (te->kind.tag)\n                        {\n                            TypeKind::U8 => { return !negated && v <= 255; },\n                            TypeKind::I8 => { return negated ? (v <= 128) : (v <= 127); },\n                            TypeKind::Char => { return !negated; },\n                            TypeKind::U16 => { return !negated && v <= 65535; },\n                            TypeKind::I16 => { return negated ? (v <= 32768) : (v <= 32767); },\n                            TypeKind::U32 => { return !negated && v <= 4294967295; },\n                            TypeKind::I32 => { return negated ? (v <= 2147483648) : (v <= 2147483647); },\n                            else => { return true; },\n                        }\n                    }\n                }\n                /* char literals are untyped: they adopt any integer target\n                 * type (`i32 c = '\\n'`, `u8 b = '0'`). The `char` type\n                 * itself (UTF-32) does NOT implicitly convert to ints. */\n                if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::CharLit)\n                {\n                    if (self.integerType(targetTy)) return true;\n                }\n                if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::FloatLit)\n                {\n                    TypeEntry* te = targetTy != 0 ? self.ctx->types + targetTy : null;\n                    if (te != null && (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::F32 || te->kind.tag == TypeKind::F64)) return true;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        /* function name → fn-pointer field/param (`T { .alloc = _foo }`,\n         * fn-pointer arguments): fn symbols carry their return type, so\n         * compatible() alone can never match a FnPtr target */\n        if (value.index != 0 && targetTy != 0)\n        {\n            /* typedef'd function pointers (`typedef SignalHandler =\n             * void(i32)`) are Named at the use site; resolve the alias\n             * before the FnPtr shape check */\n            Ty fpt = self.resolveScalarAlias(targetTy);\n            TypeEntry* tte = self.ctx->types + fpt;\n            if (tte->kind.tag == TypeKind::FnPtr)\n            {\n                Node* vn2 = self.ctx->nodes + value.index;\n                if (vn2->kind.tag == NodeKind::Expr && vn2->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.tag == ExprKind::Ident)\n                {\n                    Symbol* vs = self.lookupAt(vn2->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.payload.Ident.name, value);\n                    if (vs != null && vs->kind == 2) return true;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    /* is the value an integer (literal or typed) that a pointer target\n     * must reject; the shape checkAssign turns into TC-0009 */\n    bool intToPtrAssign(NodeId value, Ty fromTy, Ty targetTy)\n    {\n        if (fromTy == 0 || targetTy == 0 || value.index == 0) return false;\n        if (!self.pointerLike(targetTy)) return false;\n        if (self.integerType(fromTy)) return true;\n        Node* vn = self.ctx->nodes + value.index;\n        if (vn->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return false;\n        Expr* ev = &vn->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::IntLit) return true;\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Neg)\n        {\n            NodeId inner = ev->kind.payload.Neg.expr;\n            if (inner.index == 0) return false;\n            Node* nin = self.ctx->nodes + inner.index;\n            return nin->kind.tag == NodeKind::Expr && nin->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.tag == ExprKind::IntLit;\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    // `x.payload` access node (inside a field chain)\n    bool isPayloadAccessNode(NodeId objId)\n    {\n        if (objId.index == 0) return false;\n        Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + objId.index;\n        if (n->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return false;\n        Expr* e = &n->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (e->kind.tag == ExprKind::Field)\n            return self.ctx->internEqHashLen(e->kind.payload.Field.field, 0x330F77A5, 7); /* FNV(\"payload\") */\n        if (e->kind.tag == ExprKind::DerefField)\n            return self.ctx->internEqHashLen(e->kind.payload.DerefField.field, 0x330F77A5, 7); /* FNV(\"payload\") */\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    Str fieldAccessName(NodeId id)\n    {\n        Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + id.index;\n        Expr* e = &n->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (e->kind.tag == ExprKind::Field) return e->kind.payload.Field.field;\n        return e->kind.payload.DerefField.field;\n    }\n\n    NodeId fieldAccessObj(NodeId id)\n    {\n        Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + id.index;\n        Expr* e = &n->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (e->kind.tag == ExprKind::Field) return e->kind.payload.Field.obj;\n        return e->kind.payload.DerefField.obj;\n    }\n\n    // `x.payload.Case.field` leaf: the object access is `x.payload.Case`\n    bool isVariantCaseAccess(NodeId objId)\n    {\n        if (objId.index == 0) return false;\n        Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + objId.index;\n        if (n->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return false;\n        Expr* e = &n->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (e->kind.tag != ExprKind::Field && e->kind.tag != ExprKind::DerefField) return false;\n        return self.isPayloadAccessNode(self.fieldAccessObj(objId));\n    }\n\n    /* assignCompatible + the one diagnostic it cannot phrase itself:\n     * int→pointer is TC-0009 (always reported; --allow-int-ptr makes it\n     * non-fatal). Returns false only for ordinary mismatches; the\n     * caller then emits its generic message on the same node. */\n    bool checkAssign(NodeId value, Ty fromTy, Ty targetTy)\n    {\n        if (self.assignCompatible(value, fromTy, targetTy)) return true;\n        /* `kind.tag = V::Case`: a bare variant case into the tag int; the\n         * backend writes the ordinal */\n        if (self.integerType(self.stripType(targetTy)) && self.isVariantNamedTy(fromTy)) return true;\n        if (self.intToPtrAssign(value, fromTy, targetTy))\n        {\n            self.intToPtrDiag(value);\n            return true;\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    Ty assignTargetType(NodeId target)\n    {\n        Ty t = self.exprType(target);\n        if (t != 0 && target.index != 0)\n        {\n            Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + target.index;\n            TypeEntry* te = self.ctx->types + t;\n            if (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Pointer &&\n                n->kind.tag == NodeKind::Expr &&\n                n->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.tag == ExprKind::Ident &&\n                self.ctx->internEqHashLen(n->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.payload.Ident.name, 0x645BA277, 4)) /* FNV(\"self\") */\n            {\n                // `self = x` writes through the implicit self pointer in the C backend\n                return te->kind.payload.Pointer.base;\n            }\n        }\n        return t;\n    }\n\n    /* binary result typing, roughly in order: variant-vs-tag comparisons,\n     * pointer arithmetic (`+`, `-`, and pointer-minus-pointer below), then\n     * scalar rules. isSub only matters for `-` (byte distance between\n     * pointers). nothing here is checked \"forward\"; each operand is typed,\n     * then the pair decides the result */\n    bool checkBinary(NodeId id, NodeId left, NodeId right, bool isSub)\n    {\n        if (!self.checkExpr(left)) return false;\n        if (!self.checkExpr(right)) return false;\n        Ty leftType = self.exprType(left);\n        Ty rightType = self.exprType(right);\n        // an untyped side (null) borrows the other side's type\n        if (leftType == 0) leftType = rightType;\n        if (rightType == 0) rightType = leftType;\n        /* `v.tag == V::Case`: a variant value compared against its tag\n         * int; the backend lowers the case side to the ordinal.\n         * isVariantNamedTy strips pointers, so guard against pointer\n         * operands: `variantPtr + i` is pointer arithmetic, not a tag\n         * comparison, and must not become i32 */\n        if (self.integerType(leftType) && !self.pointerLike(rightType) && self.isVariantNamedTy(rightType))\n        {\n            self.setExprType(id, self.i32Type());\n            return true;\n        }\n        if (self.integerType(rightType) && !self.pointerLike(leftType) && self.isVariantNamedTy(leftType))\n        {\n            self.setExprType(id, self.i32Type());\n            return true;\n        }\n        /* `p - q` with both sides pointers; byte distance (usize); the\n         * pointer-preserving rule below only covers `p - i` */\n        if (isSub && self.pointerLike(leftType) && self.pointerLike(rightType))\n        {\n            self.setExprType(id, self.usizeType());\n            return true;\n        }\n        /* no implicit scalar conversion in operators either: same type,\n         * or a literal adopting the typed side (`i < 10`, `8 + (u32)x`);\n         * mixed typed operands need an explicit cast on one side */\n        if (self.integerType(leftType) && self.integerType(rightType))\n        {\n            bool lLit = left.index != 0 && self.isIntLitNode(left);\n            bool rLit = right.index != 0 && self.isIntLitNode(right);\n            if (self.sameType(leftType, rightType)) { self.setExprType(id, leftType); return true; }\n            /* two operands with only provisional types (literals and\n             * literal-only arithmetic like `0x7FFF... - 1`): the wider\n             * side wins so nothing has to be typed by hand */\n            bool lGen = lLit || (left.index != 0 && self.isConstIntExpr(left));\n            bool rGen = rLit || (right.index != 0 && self.isConstIntExpr(right));\n            if (lGen && rGen)\n            {\n                u32 lw = self.intWidth(leftType);\n                u32 rw = self.intWidth(rightType);\n                if (lw > rw) self.setExprType(id, leftType);\n                else if (rw > lw) self.setExprType(id, rightType);\n                else if (!self.intSigned(leftType) && self.intSigned(rightType)) self.setExprType(id, leftType);\n                else self.setExprType(id, rightType);\n                return true;\n            }\n            /* a generic side (literal or literal-only arithmetic) adopts\n             * the typed side's integer type */\n            if (lGen && !rGen && (!lLit || self.intLitAdoptsTo(left, rightType))) { self.setExprType(id, rightType); return true; }\n            if (rGen && !lGen && (!rLit || self.intLitAdoptsTo(right, leftType))) { self.setExprType(id, leftType); return true; }\n            /* usize/isize are the platform word types; compatible() already\n             * treats them as mutually assignable with u64/i64 (C size_t vs\n             * uint64_t). Use that same rule here so `i < v.count` where i\n             * is usize and v.count is u64 works without a cast. */\n            if (self.compatible(leftType, rightType)) { self.setExprType(id, rightType); return true; }\n            if (self.compatible(rightType, leftType)) { self.setExprType(id, leftType); return true; }\n            /* char-family scalar mixing: `u8`/`i8`/`cchar` are the C\n             * byte types; like C's integer promotion they mix in scalar\n             * position the same way compatible()'s charFamily rule already\n             * lets them mix in assignment/argument position. The wider\n             * side wins the result type. coral `char` (UTF-32) is not in\n             * the family; char literals still adopt the other operand's\n             * integer type through the untyped-literal rule below. */\n            if (self.charFamily(leftType) && self.charFamily(rightType))\n            {\n                if (self.intWidth(leftType) >= self.intWidth(rightType)) self.setExprType(id, leftType);\n                else self.setExprType(id, rightType);\n                return true;\n            }\n            /* char literals are untyped: they adopt the other operand's\n             * integer type (`c == '\\n'` where c is i32: the literal '\\n'\n             * becomes i32, the `char` type itself does not convert). */\n            bool lCLit = left.index != 0 && self.isCharLitNode(left);\n            bool rCLit = right.index != 0 && self.isCharLitNode(right);\n            if (lCLit && !rLit && self.integerType(rightType)) { self.setExprType(id, rightType); return true; }\n            if (rCLit && !lLit && self.integerType(leftType)) { self.setExprType(id, leftType); return true; }\n            self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaTypeMismatch, id,\n                self.typeMismatchMsg(\"binary operand types\", leftType, rightType));\n            self.setExprType(id, leftType);\n            return true;\n        }\n        if (self.floatType(leftType) && self.floatType(rightType))\n        {\n            if (self.sameType(leftType, rightType)) { self.setExprType(id, leftType); return true; }\n            bool lFLit = left.index != 0 && self.isFloatLitNode(left);\n            bool rFLit = right.index != 0 && self.isFloatLitNode(right);\n            if (lFLit && !rFLit) { self.setExprType(id, rightType); return true; }\n            if (rFLit && !lFLit) { self.setExprType(id, leftType); return true; }\n            self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaTypeMismatch, id,\n                self.typeMismatchMsg(\"binary operand types\", leftType, rightType));\n            self.setExprType(id, leftType);\n            return true;\n        }\n        /* pointer arithmetic: `p + i`, `i + p`, `p - i`, `arr + n`; result\n         * keeps the pointer side (C semantics; the backend lowers it natively) */\n        Ty lpTy = self.ptrArithType(leftType);\n        if (lpTy != 0 && (self.integerType(rightType) || (right.index != 0 && self.isIntLitNode(right))))\n        {\n            self.setExprType(id, lpTy);\n            return true;\n        }\n        Ty rpTy = self.ptrArithType(rightType);\n        if (rpTy != 0 && (self.integerType(leftType) || (left.index != 0 && self.isIntLitNode(left))))\n        {\n            self.setExprType(id, rpTy);\n            return true;\n        }\n        /* literal on the left, typed integer on the right: the literal\n         * takes the other side's type (`8 + (u32)x` → u32, not i32) */\n        if (left.index != 0 && self.isIntLitNode(left) && self.integerType(rightType))\n        {\n            self.setExprType(id, rightType);\n            return true;\n        }\n        if (!self.compatible(leftType, rightType) && !self.compatible(rightType, leftType))\n        {\n            /* int literal vs float gets the same leniency as initializers\n             * (assignCompatible's IntLit arm): `x > 0`, `0.5 * n`; the\n             * literal behaves as the float operand; result = the float side */\n            if (left.index != 0 && self.isIntLitNode(left) && self.floatType(rightType))\n            { self.setExprType(id, rightType); return true; }\n            if (right.index != 0 && self.isIntLitNode(right) && self.floatType(leftType))\n            { self.setExprType(id, leftType); return true; }\n            self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaTypeMismatch, id,\n                self.typeMismatchMsg(\"binary operand types\", leftType, rightType));\n        }\n        self.setExprType(id, leftType);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    /* True when the node is an integer literal (looking through unary\n     * negation). Does not inspect the unsigned suffix. */\n    bool isIntLitNode(NodeId id)\n    {\n        if (id.index == 0) return false;\n        Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + id.index;\n        if (n->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return false;\n        Expr* ev = &n->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Neg) return self.isIntLitNode(ev->kind.payload.Neg.expr);\n        return ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::IntLit;\n    }\n\n    /* True when the node is a compile-time constant integer expression:\n     * an integer literal, a char literal, or a binary op whose both\n     * operands are themselves const-int expressions (`16 + 1`, `'a' - 1`).\n     * These are generic; they adopt the expected type at the use site. */\n    bool isConstIntExpr(NodeId id) { return self.isConstIntExprD(id, 0); }\n\n    bool isConstIntExprD(NodeId id, u32 depth)\n    {\n        if (id.index == 0 || depth > 24) return false;\n        Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + id.index;\n        if (n->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return false;\n        Expr* ev = &n->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::IntLit) return true;\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::CharLit) return true;\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Neg) return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Neg.expr, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Add) return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Add.left, depth + 1) && self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Add.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Sub) return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Sub.left, depth + 1) && self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Sub.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Mul) return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Mul.left, depth + 1) && self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Mul.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Div) return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Div.left, depth + 1) && self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Div.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Mod) return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Mod.left, depth + 1) && self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Mod.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::BitAnd) return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.BitAnd.left, depth + 1) && self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.BitAnd.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::BitOr) return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.BitOr.left, depth + 1) && self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.BitOr.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::BitXor) return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.BitXor.left, depth + 1) && self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.BitXor.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Shl) return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Shl.left, depth + 1) && self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Shl.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Shr) return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Shr.left, depth + 1) && self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Shr.right, depth + 1);\n        // a reference to an int constant counts: `u64 x = r ? y : INT64_MAX`\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Ident)\n        {\n            Symbol* sym = self.lookupAt(ev->kind.payload.Ident.name, id);\n            if (sym != null && sym->declaration.index != 0)\n            {\n                Node* dn = self.ctx->nodes + sym->declaration.index;\n                if (dn->kind.tag == NodeKind::Decl)\n                {\n                    Decl* dd = &dn->kind.payload.Decl.value;\n                    if (dd->kind.tag == DeclKind::Constant) return self.isConstIntExprD(dd->kind.payload.Constant.value, depth + 1);\n                }\n            }\n            return false;\n        }\n        /* a ternary over const-int branches is int-generic too; the\n         * condition does not affect the result's type */\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Ternary)\n        {\n            return self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Ternary.thenExpr, depth + 1) &&\n                   self.isConstIntExprD(ev->kind.payload.Ternary.elseExpr, depth + 1);\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    /* True when a const-int expr contains a `u`-suffixed literal anywhere\n     * (or references an unsigned-typed int constant): such an expr is\n     * generic for unsigned targets only, matching the bare-literal rule. */\n    bool hasUnsignedSuffix(NodeId id) { return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(id, 0); }\n\n    bool hasUnsignedSuffixD(NodeId id, u32 depth)\n    {\n        if (id.index == 0 || depth > 24) return false;\n        Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + id.index;\n        if (n->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return false;\n        Expr* ev = &n->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::IntLit) return (ev->kind.payload.IntLit.flags & 1) != 0;\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::CharLit) return false;\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Neg) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Neg.expr, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Add) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Add.left, depth + 1) || self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Add.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Sub) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Sub.left, depth + 1) || self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Sub.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Mul) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Mul.left, depth + 1) || self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Mul.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Div) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Div.left, depth + 1) || self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Div.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Mod) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Mod.left, depth + 1) || self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Mod.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::BitAnd) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.BitAnd.left, depth + 1) || self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.BitAnd.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::BitOr) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.BitOr.left, depth + 1) || self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.BitOr.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::BitXor) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.BitXor.left, depth + 1) || self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.BitXor.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Shl) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Shl.left, depth + 1) || self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Shl.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Shr) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Shr.left, depth + 1) || self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Shr.right, depth + 1);\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Ident)\n        {\n            Symbol* sym = self.lookupAt(ev->kind.payload.Ident.name, id);\n            if (sym != null)\n            {\n                if (sym->typeNode != 0 && self.integerType(sym->typeNode) && !self.intSigned(sym->typeNode)) return true;\n                if (sym->declaration.index != 0)\n                {\n                    Node* dn = self.ctx->nodes + sym->declaration.index;\n                    if (dn->kind.tag == NodeKind::Decl)\n                    {\n                        Decl* dd = &dn->kind.payload.Decl.value;\n                        if (dd->kind.tag == DeclKind::Constant) return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(dd->kind.payload.Constant.value, depth + 1);\n                    }\n                }\n            }\n            return false;\n        }\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Ternary)\n        {\n            return self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Ternary.thenExpr, depth + 1) ||\n                   self.hasUnsignedSuffixD(ev->kind.payload.Ternary.elseExpr, depth + 1);\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    /* True when the node is a character literal. Char literals are untyped:\n     * they carry a u32 codepoint value but adopt the other operand's\n     * integer type in comparisons/assignments (`c == '\\n'` where c is i32).\n     * The `char` type itself (UTF-32 codepoint) does NOT implicitly convert\n     * to/from integer types; only the literal does. */\n    bool isCharLitNode(NodeId id)\n    {\n        if (id.index == 0) return false;\n        Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + id.index;\n        if (n->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return false;\n        Expr* ev = &n->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        return ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::CharLit;\n    }\n\n    // True when the literal node carries the unsigned suffix (flags & 1).\n    bool isUnsignedIntLit(NodeId id)\n    {\n        if (id.index == 0) return false;\n        Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + id.index;\n        if (n->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return false;\n        Expr* ev = &n->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        if (ev->kind.tag == ExprKind::Neg) return self.isUnsignedIntLit(ev->kind.payload.Neg.expr);\n        if (ev->kind.tag != ExprKind::IntLit) return false;\n        return (ev->kind.payload.IntLit.flags & 1) != 0;\n    }\n\n    /* A literal adopts the other operand's type, but an unsigned-suffixed\n     * literal only adopts unsigned types (it is generic for unsigned only). */\n    bool intLitAdoptsTo(NodeId id, Ty targetType)\n    {\n        if (!self.isIntLitNode(id)) return false;\n        if (self.isUnsignedIntLit(id)) return !self.intSigned(targetType);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    /* A bare (unsuffixed) integer literal is generic: it adopts the other\n     * operand's type in operators, initializers, and comparisons. `-4095`\n     * parses as Neg(IntLit), so we look through the unary negation. A literal\n     * carrying the unsigned suffix is generic for unsigned types only. */\n\n    bool isFloatLitNode(NodeId id)\n    {\n        if (id.index == 0) return false;\n        Node* n = self.ctx->nodes + id.index;\n        if (n->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return false;\n        return n->kind.payload.Expr.value.kind.tag == ExprKind::FloatLit;\n    }\n\n    /* Pointer or rawptr, looking through Const/Comptime wrappers; the\n     * pointer side of `p + i` keeps its own (possibly const) type */\n    bool pointerLike(Ty typeNode)\n    {\n        while (typeNode != 0)\n        {\n            TypeEntry* te = self.ctx->types + typeNode;\n            if (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Pointer || te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Rawptr) return true;\n            if (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Const) typeNode = te->kind.payload.Const.base;\n            else if (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Comptime) typeNode = te->kind.payload.Comptime.base;\n            else return false;\n        }\n        return false;\n    }\n\n    /* result type of pointer arithmetic: the pointer side itself, or the\n     * decayed Pointer(T) for arrays (`stackBuf + n`); 0 when not pointer-like */\n    Ty ptrArithType(Ty typeNode)\n    {\n        Ty orig = typeNode;\n        while (typeNode != 0)\n        {\n            TypeEntry* te = self.ctx->types + typeNode;\n            if (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Pointer || te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Rawptr) return orig;\n            if (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Array)\n            {\n                TypeKind pk;\n                pk = TypeKind::Pointer{ .base = te->kind.payload.Array.base };\n                return self.allocType(pk);\n            }\n            if (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Const) typeNode = te->kind.payload.Const.base;\n            else if (te->kind.tag == TypeKind::Comptime) typeNode = te->kind.payload.Comptime.base;\n            else return 0;\n        }\n        return 0;\n    }\n\n    bool checkBinaryBool(NodeId id, NodeId left, NodeId right)\n    {\n        if (!self.checkBinary(id, left, right, false)) return false;\n        self.setExprType(id, self.boolType());\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    /* `&&` / `||`; C truthiness: bool, any integer, or a pointer on\n     * either side (`!inStack && alloc->fallback`), result always bool.\n     * checkBinary's strict operand compatibility does not apply here. */\n    bool checkCondBinary(NodeId id, NodeId left, NodeId right)\n    {\n        if (!self.checkExpr(left)) return false;\n        if (!self.checkExpr(right)) return false;\n        Ty lt = self.exprType(left);\n        Ty rt = self.exprType(right);\n        if (lt != 0 && lt != self.boolType() && !self.integerType(lt) && !self.pointerLike(lt))\n            self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaTypeMismatch, id, self.typeMismatchMsg(\"left operand of &&/||\", lt, self.boolType()));\n        if (rt != 0 && rt != self.boolType() && !self.integerType(rt) && !self.pointerLike(rt))\n            self.semaErrorNode(ErrorCode::SemaTypeMismatch, id, self.typeMismatchMsg(\"right operand of &&/||\", rt, self.boolType()));\n        self.setExprType(id, self.boolType());\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    /* ── the walk ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */\n\n    /* entry point: type every subexpression depth-first, write the result\n     * back via setExprType. id 0 and non-expr nodes pass through silently;\n     * the parser leaves holes (e->g. an omitted then-branch). */\n    bool checkExpr(NodeId id)\n    {\n        if (id.index == 0) return true;\n        Node* node = self.ctx->nodes + id.index;\n        if (node->kind.tag != NodeKind::Expr) return true;\n        Expr* expr = &node->kind.payload.Expr.value;\n        switch (expr->kind.tag)\n        {\n            ExprKind::IntLit => {\n                u64 v = expr->kind.payload.IntLit.value;\n                u8 flags = expr->kind.payload.IntLit.flags;\n                bool isUnsigned = (flags & 1) != 0;\n                // bit 2 is the C-style long/long-long suffix (`1ULL`, `4L`).\n                // It selects a 64-bit type regardless of magnitude.\n                bool isLong = (flags & 4) != 0;\n                Ty t;\n                // no suffix: first type it fits wins, i32 → i64 → u64.\n                if (isUnsigned)\n                {\n                    /* `u` suffix: unsigned literal. Typed as the widest\n                     * unsigned type it fits in (u64 for anything that fits\n                     * in 64 bits); the literal-adoption rule widens it\n                     * further to usize when the other operand